259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (The pressing issue we aim to tackle is the rising incidents of children getting lost, followed, or abducted, causing immense distress among parents who fear for their children's safety. Recognizing this widespread problem, Safe Where embarked on a mission to create innovative and interactive bracelets that not only ensure the security of children but also alleviate the stress parents experience when their child is missing. Our motivation stems from our desire to provide a safer environment for the future generation of children.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (A significant challenge we faced was convincing children to wear our safety bracelet. Through collaborative brainstorming sessions with our mentors, we constructed a unique approach. Safe Where has implemented tracking endangered species into our solution. Now, children can not only be tracked by their parents but can also engage with the bracelet by tracking the journey their new animal best friend. This innovative feature establishes a meaningful connection between the child and the endangered species, fostering a sense of bond and responsibility.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (While our product primarily addresses the aforementioned issues, our research has unveiled additional benefits. In addition to enhancing child safety, our solution spreads awareness about endangered species around the world and supports their conservation efforts. Furthermore, to combat the issues we are tackling, the Safe Where team donates part of our proceeds to The Polaris Project and an anti-human trafficking organization, making our company more comprehensive and impactful.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
