/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (The National Center for Missing and Exploited Children reported a 71% effectiveness rate for Amber Alerts in familial cases as of 2021.  However, in instances involving abduction by strangers, Amber Alerts only yield a 13% success rate in recovering a child within three hours of the abduction \(Griffin, 2021\).  In essence, Amber alerts are significantly less effective in cases of child abduction by strangers.  When children face these dangerous situations, it is imperative to have effective solutions in place to safeguard and rescue them, offer parents peace of mind, and reduce the likelihood of children falling into perilous situations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
