285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (Current location tracking bracelets with non-removable trackers and other band types are also not kid-friendly due to the huge size of the tracker, uncomfortableness, and lack of discreetness. All existing trackers also need a phone to function properly. As young children are the ones who are using such devices, and only 53% of children up to age 11 own a phone, it becomes infeasible for children without phones to be tracked, accounting for 47% of children \(NPR.org, 2019\). This leaves the market with a high demand for discreet tracking devices without the child needing a phone.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [13]
>>
